WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.713
How do you get there when
the target is years away?

2
00:00:02.713 --> 00:00:04.587
Make the case by elimination.

3
00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:10.138
The legacy telecom contracts
had all ended by May 31, 2026.

4
00:00:10.138 --> 00:00:11.981
The hairpin is still permitted,

5
00:00:11.981 --> 00:00:16.237
but CISA's own guidebook says it raised
the cost of using cloud services.

6
00:00:16.237 --> 00:00:21.008
A new access point is a capital
commitment, VPN backhaul is a hairpin,

7
00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:25.863
and Microsoft no longer recommends
ExpressRoute for Microsoft 365.

8
00:00:25.863 --> 00:00:27.659
What's left is local breakout,

9
00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:30.951
a cloud security stack and
a branch-edge policy layer.

10
00:00:30.951 --> 00:00:37.051
Meanwhile three deadlines
compete for the same staff:

11
00:00:37.051 --> 00:00:44.100
the M-26-14 logging plan, the M-26-15
post-quantum plan and BOD 26-04.

12
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.662
BOD 26-02 is the fork.

13
00:00:47.662 --> 00:00:53.310
End-of-support edge devices must be
off agency networks by about August 5,

14
00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.851
2027, so a refresh happens anyway.

15
00:00:55.851 --> 00:00:59.625
Tell whoever scopes it, in
writing, what the target needs.

16
00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.306
Like-for-like spends the
same money and closes

17
00:01:02.306 --> 00:01:04.820
the question for the
life of the equipment.
